== Mechanics Mods

Mods that introduce new gameplay systems and deepen existing mechanics. Every card is verified against its Nexus Mods page (decision register in STATUS.md).

=== Overhaul

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/8222")[*Royal Galaxy - A Starfield Revamp And Cut Content Restoration*]

A "vanilla+" overhaul and the wave's anchor: buffs Terrormorphs and Ashta, raises enemy spawn counts, reworks the economy and vendor credits, improves loot, expands POIs and weather, and restores cut content — while editing vanilla records to stay broadly compatible.

- *Author:* JaeDL
- *Version:* 4.0 (updated 2026-04-19)
- *Dependencies:* None (follow its load-order instructions)
- *System Impact:* Major — combat, economy, exploration

=== Survival

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/6890")[*Starvival - Immersive Survival Addon*]

A deep, modular survival system: hunger, thirst, and fatigue needs; ship fuel and ammo consumption; environmental hazards; crew morale and pay; and expanded addictions/adrenaline. Every module is toggleable in its in-game configuration book.

- *Author:* lKocMoHaBTl
- *Version:* 12.5.0 (updated 2026-08-08)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Major — survival, economy, ship management
- *Notes:* Punishing by default; disable modules you don't want. Don't stack with another survival overhaul.

=== Combat

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/162")[*Weapons of Fate (Ballistics Overhaul)*]

Adds bullet drop and visible weapon tracers for a harder-edged shooter feel, with negligible performance cost.

- *Author:* Seb263
- *Version:* 1.1.1 (updated 2023-10-26)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Combat ballistics — changes how ranged weapons feel, not their stats

=== Crafting

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/6074")[*Legendary Module Recycler*]

Adds a recycler (buildable at outposts, ships, and homes; a permanent one is in the Lodge basement) that strips legendary effects from loot you already found and lets you apply them to gear you prefer.

- *Author:* JonathanOstrus
- *Version:* 2.12 (updated 2026-05-11)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Crafting/items — only recycles effects you have legitimately looted, so it is not a free spawn

=== Exploration

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/10825")[*POI Variations - No More Duplicates*]

Generates multiple variations of vanilla POIs (different loot, enemy placement, clutter) and restricts lore-heavy locations to appear only once, cutting the repetition of repeated dungeons.

- *Author:* PlatinumPoster
- *Version:* 1.03 (updated 2026-08-04)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Exploration — POI generation rules

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/13041")[*Unique POI Names*]

Replaces generic labels ("Cave", "Industrial Outpost") with unique, descriptive names so you can tell a new location from one you've already cleared.

- *Author:* paulbrock
- *Version:* 0.9 (updated 2026-04-17)
- *Dependencies:* None
- *System Impact:* Exploration — naming/readability only

=== Ship Building

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/7310")[*Ship Builder Categories (SBC)*]

A shared framework of ship-part keywords that lets multiple ship-building mods coexist without category conflicts. Load it high.

- *Author:* rux616
- *Version:* 1.21.0 (updated 2026-04-11)
- *Dependencies:* None (required by the two mods below)
- *System Impact:* Framework — no visible change on its own

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/5953")[*Better Ship Part Flips*]

Adds extra flip options to vanilla ship parts (shields, cargo, fuel tanks, grav drives, reactors, structure), unlocking far more builder layouts.

- *Author:* rux616
- *Version:* 1.3.1 (updated 2024-09-07)
- *Dependencies:* Ship Builder Categories
- *System Impact:* Ship builder — new flip variants

=== #link("https://www.nexusmods.com/starfield/mods/5698")[*Better Ship Part Snaps*]

Improves how parts snap together in the builder, allowing placements the vanilla snap rules forbid.

- *Author:* rux616
- *Version:* 1.1.0 (updated 2026-04-11)
- *Dependencies:* Ship Builder Categories
- *System Impact:* Ship builder — snap/placement rules
- *Notes:* Do not combine with Ship Module Snap Expansion (SMSEX) — they edit the same data.
